 pairs: **thickness = min(inner block's shorter side, smallest gap from the outer box to the top or left edge)**.\n\nI am not certain this is the intended rule; it is the simplest formula consistent with all five pairs.\n\n**Construction.**\n1. Find the outer object (the larger one) and the inner object (the smaller one).\n2. Compute the thickness t with the formula above.\n3. Fill the outer box grown by t on every side with the inner colour, clipped to the grid.\n4. Paste the original object back on top.\n\n**Test.** The outer ring is colour 3 at rows 6–11, columns 5–10, with a 4×4 inner block of colour 8. The gaps to the edges are 6 (top) and 5 (left), so t = min(4, 5) = 4. The output gets an 8-coloured band covering rows 2–15 and columns 1–14, with the original object kept in the middle.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    objs = sorted(objs, key=lambda o: -o[\"size\"])\n    outer, inner = objs[0], objs[1]\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = outer[\"box\"]\n    iy0, ix0, iy1, ix1 = inner[\"box\"]\n    t = min(iy1 - iy0 + 1, ix1 - ix0 + 1, y0, x0)\n    out = g.copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    a, b = max(0, y0 - t), max(0, x0 - t)\n    c, d = min(H - 1, y1 + t), min(W - 1, x1 + t)\n    out[a:c + 1, b:d + 1] = inner[\"colour\"]\n    emit(out.copy(), f\"Fill the outer box grown by {t} on every side with the inner colour {inner['colour']}.\")\n    out[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1] = g[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1]\n    emit(out, \"Restore the original framed object on top, leaving a surrounding band of thickness t.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- One formula fits all five pairs: **thickness = min(inner block's shorter side, smallest gap from the outer box to the top or left edge)**."}],"repair":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Restore the original framed object on top, leaving a surrounding band of thickness t."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Paste the original object back on top."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Restore the original framed object on top, leaving a surrounding band of thickness t."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"cac6ac352ed4ff8acf0b797b8976daca66308758ba779e0df3c87025601f5488","task_sha256":"a23008e33c624cd84a03ac7684c350e6643235a05ca43f6e9f55b8be922ab058","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
